# Metagol: learn programs that invent, recurse, and compose

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:swi_elixir, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:kino, "== 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Introduction

A few examples go in; a Prolog program comes out. This chapter uses the real
[Metagol learner](https://github.com/metagol/metagol) to invent a missing
relation, learn recursion, and transform nested lists. Read each task's
background and labels, predict a possible rule, then inspect what was learned.

Start with [Getting started](01_basic.livemd) if the wrapper is new to you.
Evaluate top to bottom in a local runtime on a [supported platform](../README.md#platforms-and-native-bundles).
Setup installs this checkout, its bundled SWI runtime, and Kino. The learner
is vendored; the complete task definitions and datasets are inline below.

